1)File System Space Management Algorithm
Aim: To monitor disk usage and automatically delete/compress log files when disk utilization exceeds 80%.

Pseudocode:
BEGIN
SET threshold = 80%
usage = GET_DISK_USAGE()
IF usage > threshold THEN
    log_files = GET_LOG_FILES()
    SORT log_files BY size DESCENDING
    FOR each file IN log_files DO
        DELETE OR COMPRESS file
        usage = GET_DISK_USAGE()
        IF usage <= threshold THEN
            BREAK
        ENDIF
    ENDFOR
ENDIF
END

Result:
The algorithm monitors disk utilization and automatically removes or compresses large log files until disk usage falls to 80% or below.


2)Priority-Based CPU Scheduling Algorithm
Aim: To improve CPU efficiency by selecting and executing processes based on their priority levels.

Pseudocode:
BEGIN
INPUT process_list
SORT process_list BY priority (highest first)
WHILE process_list IS NOT EMPTY DO
    SELECT process WITH highest priority
    ALLOCATE CPU TIME
    EXECUTE process
    IF process IS NOT COMPLETED THEN
        REDUCE priority slightly
        ADD process BACK TO process_list
        SORT process_list BY priority
    ELSE
        REMOVE process FROM process_list
    ENDIF
ENDWHILE
END

Result:
The priority-based scheduling algorithm executes high-priority processes first and gradually reduces the priority of unfinished processes to provide fair
CPU utilization.


3)RAM Resource Management Among Virtual Machines
Aim: To efficiently allocate and distribute RAM among multiple virtual machines while maintaining balanced performance.

Pseudocode:
BEGIN
SET total_RAM = 16 GB
SET host_reserved = 4 GB
available_RAM = total_RAM - host_reserved
INPUT number_of_VMs
SET min_RAM = 2 GB
FOR i = 1 TO number_of_VMs DO
    IF available_RAM >= min_RAM THEN
        ALLOCATE min_RAM TO VM[i]
        available_RAM = available_RAM - min_RAM
    ELSE
        PRINT "Insufficient memory"
    ENDIF
ENDFOR
PRINT "Remaining RAM =", available_RAM
END

Result:
The algorithm reserves 4 GB for the host system and allocates a minimum of 2 GB RAM to each virtual machine whenever sufficient memory is available.


4)Hypervisor Selection
Aim: To select the most appropriate hypervisor based on performance requirements, budget, and hardware access.

Pseudocode:
BEGIN
INPUT performance_required, budget, hardware_access
IF performance_required = HIGH AND hardware_access = TRUE THEN
    SELECT Type_1_Hypervisor
ELSE IF budget = LOW THEN
    SELECT Type_2_Hypervisor
ELSE
    SELECT Type_1_Hypervisor
ENDIF
PRINT selected_hypervisor
END

Result:
The algorithm selects a suitable hypervisor based on performance, budget, and hardware requirements.


5)CPU and Memory Resource Limiting
Aim: To regulate CPU and memory usage of applications using suitable resource-limiting mechanisms.

Pseudocode:
BEGIN
INPUT application_list
FOR each app IN application_list DO
    CREATE cgroup FOR app
    SET CPU limit
    SET memory limit
    ASSIGN process TO cgroup
ENDFOR
PRINT "CPU and memory limits applied"
END

Result:
The algorithm creates a control group for each application and assigns CPU and memory limits to ensure balanced and efficient resource utilization.
